<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xml:lang="en"><generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="4.4.1">Jekyll</generator><link href="https://sara-02.github.io/feed.xml" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml"/><link href="https://sara-02.github.io/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" hreflang="en"/><updated>2026-10-15T15:49:55+00:00</updated><id>https://sara-02.github.io/feed.xml</id><title type="html">Sarah Masud</title><subtitle>NLP | AI | Social Computing.</subtitle><entry><title type="html">Bookstores I have visited</title><link href="https://sara-02.github.io/writings/2026/bookstores/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Bookstores I have visited"/><published>2026-10-15T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-10-15T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://sara-02.github.io/writings/2026/bookstores</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://sara-02.github.io/writings/2026/bookstores/"><![CDATA[<p>Inspired by my friend Shadab’s musings on <a href="https://dufferzafar.com/2021/what-would-i-do-in-london/">what he would do in London</a>, I decided to put together a list of bookstores I have visited and purchased from around the world. I compiled this retrospectively in Oct 2026 and will update it regularly.</p> <p><strong>Delhi</strong></p> <ol> <li>All the second-hand book sellers, NFC</li> <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Faqir+Chand+%26+Sons%2C+Khan+Market%2C+New+Delhi">Faqir Chand &amp; Sons</a>, Khan Market</li> <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Bahrisons+Booksellers%2C+Khan+Market%2C+New+Delhi">Bahrisons</a>, Khan Market</li> <li>Delhi Book Fair, Pragati Maidan</li> <li>International Book Fair, Pragati Maidan</li> </ol> <p><strong>Bangalore</strong></p> <ol> <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Atta+Galatta%2C+Koramangala%2C+Bengaluru">Atta Galatta</a>, Koramangala</li> <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Nexus+Mall+%28formerly+Forum+Mall%29%2C+Koramangala%2C+Bengaluru">Landmark</a>, Forum Mall, Koramangala</li> <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Crossword+Bookstore%2C+Nexus+Whitefield+%28formerly+Forum+Neighbourhood+Mall%29%2C+Whitefield+Main+Road%2C+Bengaluru">Crossword</a>, Forum Neighbourhood Mall, Whitefield</li> </ol> <p><strong>Copenhagen</strong></p> <ol> <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Borg+Literature%2C+N%C3%B8rreport%2C+Copenhagen">Borg Literature</a>, Nørreport</li> <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Bog+%26+id%C3%A9+Amagerbrogade%2C+Copenhagen">Bog &amp; idé</a>, Amagerbro</li> <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Arnold+Busck%2C+K%C3%B8bmagergade%2C+Copenhagen">Arnold Busck</a>, Nørreport</li> <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Politikens+Boghal%2C+R%C3%A5dhuspladsen+37%2C+K%C3%B8benhavn">Politikens Boghal</a>, Rådhuspladsen</li> <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Tranquebar%2C+Borgergade+14%2C+K%C3%B8benhavn">Tranquebar</a>, Borgergade</li> </ol> <p><strong>Malmö</strong></p> <ol> <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Adlibris%2C+S%C3%B6dra+F%C3%B6rstadsgatan+32%2C+211+43+Malm%C3%B6">Adlibris</a>, Södra Förstadsgatan</li> </ol> <p><strong>Paris</strong></p> <ol> <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Shakespeare+and+Company%2C+37+Rue+de+la+B%C3%BBcherie%2C+Paris">Shakespeare and Company</a>, Latin Quarter</li> <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Librairie+Galignani%2C+224+Rue+de+Rivoli%2C+Paris">Galignani</a>, Rue de Rivoli</li> </ol> <p><strong>Geneva</strong></p> <ol> <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Librairie+Atmosph%C3%A8re%2C+Rue+Saint-L%C3%A9ger+11%2C+1205+Gen%C3%A8ve">Librairie Atmosphère</a>, Rue Saint-Léger</li> <li><a href="https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&amp;query=Illibrairie%2C+Grand-Rue+20%2C+1204+Gen%C3%A8ve">Illibrairie</a>, Grand-Rue</li> </ol>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="notes"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Inspired by my friend Shadab’s musings on what he would do in London, I decided to put together a list of bookstores I have visited and purchased from around the world. I compiled this retrospectively in Oct 2026 and will update it regularly.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">An ode to CopeNLU</title><link href="https://sara-02.github.io/writings/2026/an-ode-to-copenlu/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="An ode to CopeNLU"/><published>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2026-05-29T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://sara-02.github.io/writings/2026/an-ode-to-copenlu</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://sara-02.github.io/writings/2026/an-ode-to-copenlu/"><![CDATA[<p>Published on The Messier (WordPress): <a href="https://themessier.wordpress.com/2026/05/29/an-ode-to-copenlu/">An ode to CopeNLU</a>.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="poems"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Published on The Messier (WordPress): An ode to CopeNLU.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">To KG or not to KG, that is the question!</title><link href="https://sara-02.github.io/writings/2025/to-kg-or-not-to-kg/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="To KG or not to KG, that is the question!"/><published>2025-08-20T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-08-20T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://sara-02.github.io/writings/2025/to-kg-or-not-to-kg</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://sara-02.github.io/writings/2025/to-kg-or-not-to-kg/"><![CDATA[<p>Published in ACM SIGMOD Blog: <a href="https://wp.sigmod.org/?p=3833">To KG or not to KG, that is the question!</a>.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="invited"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Published in ACM SIGMOD Blog: To KG or not to KG, that is the question!.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">GenAI is the new Godman in India</title><link href="https://sara-02.github.io/writings/2025/genai-is-the-new-godman-in-india/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="GenAI is the new Godman in India"/><published>2025-01-01T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2025-01-01T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://sara-02.github.io/writings/2025/genai-is-the-new-godman-in-india</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://sara-02.github.io/writings/2025/genai-is-the-new-godman-in-india/"><![CDATA[<p>Published in Digital Futures Lab: Human in the Loop: <a href="https://loop.digitalfutureslab.in/open-call-stories/genai-is-the-new-godman-in-india">GenAI is the new Godman in India</a>.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="invited"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Published in Digital Futures Lab: Human in the Loop: GenAI is the new Godman in India.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">Handling Bias in Toxic Speech Detection: A Survey</title><link href="https://sara-02.github.io/writings/2022/handling-bias-in-toxic-speech-detection/" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="Handling Bias in Toxic Speech Detection: A Survey"/><published>2022-03-14T00:00:00+00:00</published><updated>2022-03-14T00:00:00+00:00</updated><id>https://sara-02.github.io/writings/2022/handling-bias-in-toxic-speech-detection</id><content type="html" xml:base="https://sara-02.github.io/writings/2022/handling-bias-in-toxic-speech-detection/"><![CDATA[<p>Published in Montreal AI Ethics Institute: <a href="https://montrealethics.ai/handling-bias-in-toxic-speech-detection-a-survey/">Handling Bias in Toxic Speech Detection: A Survey</a>.</p>]]></content><author><name></name></author><category term="invited"/><summary type="html"><![CDATA[Published in Montreal AI Ethics Institute: Handling Bias in Toxic Speech Detection: A Survey.]]></summary></entry><entry><title type="html">130Mg</title><link href="https://sara-02.github.io